The task and application numbers are different in each case, but the message is the same in each case.

As with Rick Aster, Several of the students have reported that attempting to deploy the app again at a different time lets them publish without the error.

Elsewhere on the internet it suggests that the mkdir - too many links error message <https://blog.nexcess.net/2012/04/27/mkdir-too-many-links-what-it-is-and-how-to-fix/> is related to there being too many subdirectories. There definitely isn't too many subdirectories in my shiny app (there is only one data subdirectory, and there are less than 10 files total in the app adding up to about 2Mb of space).

Is it possible that more people signed up through www.shinyapps.io/coursera <http://www.shinyapps.io/coursera> than expected, and too many subdirectories were created for their projects?

Ronny.

