Im a Coursera student also facing this issue. Its worth noting that the issue is NOT on your local side, ie it doesnt matter how many folders you have on your hard-drive. Shinyapps.io is apparently setting up a new folder for you when you deploy, and the volume they store the account folders in is full. I expect anyone who has published previously can keep doing so, unless its project folders not account folders. Since you mention some students able to "get through" the error, this would suggest either they had a different issue or there are several volumes it may try to put your folder on and not all of them are full yet. I would suggest to the JH@Coursera staff that the solution is NOT to fail everyone who cant post, and to the students please dont just hammer away at shineyapps.io <http://shineyapps.io>. This is a bug that they need to fix and waiting for that is the only real way around it.

